    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i keep getting an \"Access Denied\" error when my lambda function tries to write logs to this s3 bucket. i thought i had the permissions right but it's still failing. can u look at this policy and tell me what i missed?\n\n{\n  \"Version\": \"2012-10-17\",\n  \"Statement\": [\n    {\n      \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n      \"Action\": [\n        \"s3:PutObject\"\n      ],\n      \"Resource\": \"arn:aws:s3:::my-app-logs-bucket/*\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The policy you've provided looks mostly correct for allowing `PutObject` actions, which is what writing logs usually requires. However, if you're getting \"Access Denied,\" it's often not just the bucket policy; it could be the IAM Role attached to your Lambda function itself. You need to ensure that the Lambda's execution role has permissions to interact with that S3 bucket, not just that the bucket allows it. A common oversight is forgetting the necessary permissions on the principal (the Lambda role).",
